  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour reporting for all incidents including those under investigation and 72-hour customer notices. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% benchmark but exceeding it triggers only corrective action and retesting within 12 months, with no market withdrawal; per-model results go to regulators and customers but not the public. S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 3 years and retrofit to 6 years. S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months. S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with prompt notices and no serious-injury clause."
